================================================================================
              DO NOT BUILD MESA ON THE SL101 DEVICE
================================================================================

Mesa cross-compilation is MAGNITUDES faster via Docker / bwrap than building
natively on the Tegra2 ARM device.

The production build uses:
  - Alpine musl cross-compiler (armv7-alpine-linux-musleabihf-gcc)
  - bwrap sandbox with device sysroot at /mnt/sysroot
  - Mixed build: only recompile changed grate driver objects + relink
  - Base Mesa build from Sep 30 snapshot

Cross-build locations:
  work/sl101-grate-production-20261004/  — production build recipe & artifacts
  work/sl101-grate-production-20261004/production.cross — meson cross file
  work/sl101-grate-production-20261004/recipes/ — build scripts
  build/mesa-grate-clean/ — Docker-based full cross-build

The on-device meson build also produces DIFFERENT binaries because it resolves
pkg-config paths differently (e.g. links against /usr/local/lib/libdrm_tegra
instead of the sysroot's version), so even with identical source the output
binary may not work correctly.

ALWAYS use the cross-compilation path.
================================================================================
